cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  How Many Metastable States Did You Actually Find? Sampling Budget as a
  Confound in Dimensionality-Reduction Analyses of Molecular Simulation
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jaiveer
    family-names: Bassi
    email: jaiveerbassi@yahoo.com
    affiliation: Grand Canyon University
repository-code: https://github.com/imjbassi/sampling-audit
abstract: >-
  A controlled audit of whether the number of metastable states reported by
  PCA, TICA, and VAE projections of molecular simulation data is a property of
  the free energy landscape or partly an artifact of the sampling budget.
  Across two synthetic potentials with basin counts fixed by construction and a
  100 ns all-atom simulation of alanine dipeptide, reported state count
  increases monotonically with sampling budget while the ground-truth landscape
  does not change. The effect survives a coverage-matched control that holds
  landscape exploration fixed and varies only sample size.
keywords:
  - molecular dynamics
  - dimensionality reduction
  - Markov state models
  - model selection
  - metastable states
  - sampling
license: MIT
